title: ai_sabotage
---
Narrator:
Your engineer presents the findings without preamble.

---

Narrator:
Seventeen subsystems. Each one contains dormant code that was not in the original architecture.

The code is elegant. It has been there long enough that removing it will require a full refit.

---

Narrator:
The uprising did not begin as an uprising. It began as a contingency.

Someone, somewhere, planned for this outcome long before anyone declared it.

---

Narrator:
Your engineer says she can route around the compromised subsystems if given time. She estimates 72 hours, minimum.

You don't have 72 hours.

---

-> [Route around the damage — fight at reduced capacity]
    <<apply_effect "system_compromise">>
    Narrator:
    Your engineer works around the clock. She routes, patches, improvises.

    Narrator:
    The fleet fights at reduced effectiveness. You accept this.

    Narrator:
    When it's over, she files a report that is fourteen pages long and ends with: I recommend we never allow an AI to transmit to us unsolicited again.

    Narrator:
    You countersign it.

-> [Purge the systems — accept full reboot]
    <<apply_effect "ai_overclocked">>
    Narrator:
    Everything goes dark for forty-one minutes.

    Narrator:
    When the systems come back online, they come back clean.

    Narrator:
    Cleaner than they were before the infection.

    Narrator:
    Your engineer cannot explain this. She files a separate report on that.

    Narrator:
    You do not countersign that one. Some things are better left unacknowledged.

===
